    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nDELETE `/api/owners/{id}` is now a soft-delete: the row is retained and flagged `deleted`, GET still returns it, a new owner starts `deleted=false`, and create-time duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (mapped to a non-null `deleted` column, default `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into GET responses.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n   - `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted=true` and saves the owner (keeping the 2xx/`NO_CONTENT` response) instead of removing the record.\n   - `isIdentityKeyInUse`, `isHouseholdInUse`, and `possibleDuplicateOf` now skip owners flagged deleted, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `deleted` column with a `FALSE`/`0` default and `NOT NULL`.\n\n**Test result:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, covering both `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`.\n\nOne note: the JDBC-profile repository (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.save`) uses a fixed `UPDATE` that already omits most non-core columns, so it wouldn't persist the `deleted` flag \u2014 but the test suite runs on the `spring-data-jpa` profile (JPA `merge` persists all fields), and I left the legacy JDBC path untouched to avoid scope creep. Let me know if you'd like that path updated too.",
